# {{PROJECT_NAME}} - Branch Demo
# A branch arc file — reached via [goto] from the prologue, forwards to the epilogue via [goto].
# The arc chain: prologue → this file → epilogue.
# Replace the placeholder content below with a real scene: dialogue, characters, backgrounds, choices.
# Add more branch files by duplicating this file, giving it a new @scenario ID,
# and adding a [goto] in the prologue that points to it.

@scenario {{SCENARIO_PREFIX}}_branch_demo
@include {{CHARACTERS_INCLUDE}}

# ─── Scene ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Your scene starts at @label start. Write dialogue, show characters, set backgrounds.
# When the scene is done, the [goto] at the bottom forwards to the epilogue.

@label start
[show lavender center {{LAVENDER_EXPR}}]
narrator: This is {b}{{STORY_BRANCH_SCRIPT_PATH}}{/b} — a branch arc reached from the prologue via [goto].
narrator: Replace everything between @label start and the [goto] below with your own scene content.

# ─── Forward to Epilogue ────────────────────────────────────────
# This [goto] completes the arc. All branches can converge on the same epilogue,
# or you can create separate epilogue files for different routes.

[goto {{EPILOGUE_TARGET}}:start]
